The '''coat of arms of the [[Bolodun and Kuvari Islands]]''' is the national emblem of the island country. It was adopted following independence in 1926 and shares the symbolism of the [[flag of Bolodun and Kuvari|national flag]]: a red field representing the global movement for socialism, a black fourteen-pointed star representing the fourteen inhabited islands and the [[Sudanese Kaftians of the Bolodun and Kuvari Islands|Sudanese Kaftian]] people, and a yellow circle representing the [[Kuvari people]].

== Design ==

The emblem consists of a central red disc, bordered in gold and charged with the national star — a black fourteen-pointed star with a yellow circle at its centre.

== Symbolism ==

The red disc and the black star with its yellow core echo the national flag, preserving the same meanings: socialism, the fourteen inhabited islands and the Sudanese Kaftian people, and the Kuvari people at the country's heart.

